    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Definitions'>
      <repository-location id='Definitions' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/FDNCImpactAnalysis' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='text-orientation' id='dash-text_174' value='-90' />
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_1032' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='parameter-ctrl'>
          <format attr='color' value='#000000' />
          <format attr='font-size' value='9' />
          <format attr='font-weight' value='normal' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='parameter-ctrl-title'>
          <format attr='text-align' value='center' />
          <format attr='font-size' value='10' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1300' maxwidth='1366' minheight='1300' minwidth='1366' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='110337' id='3' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98310' x='845' y='1045'>
          <zone fixed-size='219' h='17384' id='813' is-fixed='true' type-v2='layout-basic' w='97944' x='918' y='1353'>
            <zone fixed-size='326' forceUpdate='true' h='16845' id='15' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='19761' x='18233' y='1815'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='20'>FDNC Impact Analysis</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='16'>Definitions</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone fixed-size='72' h='16845' id='14' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/DH Logistics Logo.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='17315' x='918' y='1815'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='16845' id='927' type-v2='empty' w='60795' x='37994' y='1815'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='0' />
                <format attr='padding' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='1' />
              <format attr='margin-top' value='6' />
              <format attr='margin-left' value='0' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone fixed-size='2' h='769' id='71' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='97944' x='918' y='18737'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              <format attr='margin-top' value='4' />
              <format attr='margin-bottom' value='4' />
              <format attr='background-color' value='#000000' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone fixed-size='974' forceUpdate='true' h='75538' id='1032' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='97944' x='918' y='19506'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>What is FDNC?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>Free Delivery for New Customers is a pricing incentive configured in DPS, where a scheme with no delivery fee is assigned only to new users. This conditional scheme in an ASA or Campaign takes higher priority than the standard scheme with no conditions.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>What is FDNTV?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>Free Delivery for New To Vertical is a pricing incentive, like FDNC, targetting users who place their first order in the Darkstore vertical, or Qcommerce verticals. Qcommerce are all verticals other than restaurants, couriers, and in this case, darkstores (as darkstore orders have their own FDNTV category)..</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>What are New Customers?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- Customers who have never placed an order before (&quot;Single FDNC&quot;)</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- Customers who have placed hup to a certain number of orders, or who placed their first order within a certain time period (&quot;Multiple FDNC&quot;). For example, the first ten orders a customer places could be considered for free delivery, or any orders placed in the first 30 days following the first order.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>What is the FDNC Impact Analysis Dashboard?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>This dashboard is used to understand how many customers qualified for Free Delivery based on new customer conditions. Of those customers, we then want to know how many were correctly granted free delivery. There are two cases we may have problems:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- False Negatives, where a customer who should have gotten free delivery did not get it.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- False Positives, where a customer who should </run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' italic='true'>not</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'> have gotten free delivery got it.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>How do we check if we applied FDNC correctly?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>We compare six data points identifying the customer for each order to understand if it was placed by the same persons and compare the results to the DPS tables: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the customer account ID in the Central Data Warehouse (CDW) orders table (also available in DPS tables, but the CDW orders tables has data stretching back farther than DPS orders tables)</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the associated customer IDs in Central Data Platform (CDP)&apos;s customers snapshots table</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the perseus ID from CDP&apos;s facts.orders table (also available in DPS tables) which identifies a specific device</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the adjust ID from CDP&apos;s facts.orders, which itself takes multiple features to create a single ID for customers</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the analytical customer ID from CDP&apos;s facts.orders table (also available in DPS tables) which also tries to use the same ID for associated users</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>- the hashed phone number from CDP&apos;s facts.orders table</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='15'>How does the data pipeline work?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>The pipeline for FDNC follows seven steps:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>1. Get all the orders placed in an ASA or Campaign that had an active customer condition at the time.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>2. Get all the customer IDs for those orders, and count orders for them in CDW&apos;s orders table.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>3. Join CDP customer snapshot data using the customer account ID.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>4. Join perseus id, adjust id, analytical customer id, and hashed phone number from CDP facts.orders table.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>5. Now that we have all the IDs associated with each order, we compare the features for the customer to the different conditional schemes for the ASA or Campaign. For example, we check if the customer should be in the new customer condition scheme using all the different IDs.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>6. Then, we compare the scheme that the order was actually selected and reported in the DPS tables to the simulated results based on all the other customer identifiers. Generally, the other identifiers will have less information than what&apos;s reported in DPS, so we don&apos;t care about these. For orders where the other identifiers show more orders, or an earlier first order than DPS, we can compare those IDs to DPS. If the scheme selected by DPS matches the simulated scheme using those other IDs, we correctly applied (or did not apply) FDNC. If there is a discrepancy, we made a mistake.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333'>7. Finally we estimate the lost delivery fees using the average delivery fee of orders placed in the same zone within the period 30 minutes before and 30 minutes after the order.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            <format attr='margin-left' value='1' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone fixed-size='57' h='2364' id='476' is-fixed='true' layout-strategy-id='distribute-evenly' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='118302' x='-220' y='0'>
